Numlore — Third-party attributions

This product uses the following third-party data sources and libraries.
The attributions below are also rendered on /credits.

----------------------------------------------------------------------

CMU Pronouncing Dictionary
  ARPAbet phonetic transcriptions for approximately 134,000 English words.
  Source: http://www.speech.cs.cmu.edu/cgi-bin/cmudict
  License: public-domain-style (see the dictionary's distribution).

Princeton WordNet 3.1
  Lexical database providing parts of speech and semantic hierarchies.
  Source: https://wordnet.princeton.edu/
  License: WordNet license (BSD-style attribution).

wordfreq
  Python library used at build time to compute Zipf word frequency.
  Used as a development dependency; not shipped in the runtime bundle.
  Source: https://github.com/rspeer/wordfreq
  License: MIT.

Brysbaert, Warriner, & Kuperman (2014)
  Concreteness ratings for 40,000 generally known English word lemmas.
  Brysbaert, M., Warriner, A. B., & Kuperman, V. (2014).
  Concreteness ratings for 40 thousand generally known English word lemmas.
  Behavior Research Methods, 46(3), 904-911.

Glyphex
  Aggregate page analytics. The only third-party script loaded by Numlore;
  used to measure page hits without recording individual user choices.
  Source: https://glyphex.io

----------------------------------------------------------------------

Vendored source files live under data/dictionaries/_sources/. They are
committed to the repository and never fetched at build time.
